WEBVTT

00:00.290 --> 00:03.890
— CLOSING CEREMONY —

00:01.280 --> 00:04.840
<i>The 6th National Youth Football Tournament's champion is</i>

00:04.840 --> 00:09.240
<i>Nankatsu SC, the representatives from Shizuoka Prefecture.</i>

00:09.240 --> 00:10.070
Here!

00:14.990 --> 00:16.960
Congratulations.

00:16.960 --> 00:18.570
Thank you very much.

00:19.440 --> 00:26.370
<i>The purple championship pennant is handed to Nankatsu SC's captain, Tsubasa Ozora.</i>

00:28.100 --> 00:30.140
We did it!

00:45.080 --> 00:50.690
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

00:45.080 --> 00:50.690
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

00:50.690 --> 00:55.740
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

00:50.690 --> 00:55.740
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

00:56.410 --> 01:01.540
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

00:56.410 --> 01:01.540
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:02.290 --> 01:09.880
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:02.290 --> 01:09.880
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:09.880 --> 01:15.650
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:09.880 --> 01:15.650
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

01:15.650 --> 01:24.150
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:15.650 --> 01:24.150
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

01:24.150 --> 01:29.940
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

01:24.150 --> 01:29.940
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

01:29.940 --> 01:35.870
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

01:29.940 --> 01:35.870
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

01:35.870 --> 01:37.410
<i>Run & Run!</i>

01:37.410 --> 01:44.700
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

01:37.410 --> 01:44.700
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

01:44.700 --> 01:47.620
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

01:44.700 --> 01:47.620
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

01:47.620 --> 01:52.550
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

01:47.620 --> 01:52.550
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:03.640 --> 02:08.770
<b><b>EPISODE 28:
TO EACH, HIS OWN DEPARTURE</b></b>

02:04.240 --> 02:09.640
<i>Captain Tsubasa Ozora hoists the championship pennant high.</i>

02:09.640 --> 02:12.770
<i>Our heartfelt congratulations go to Nankatsu SC!</i>

02:12.770 --> 02:14.900
We did it!

02:14.900 --> 02:17.030
Hooray! Hooray!

02:17.030 --> 02:18.940
You're so cool, Tsubasa!

02:18.940 --> 02:19.990
You are the best!

02:19.990 --> 02:22.950
Congratulations, Tsubasa...

02:22.950 --> 02:27.430
<i>Additionally, Tsubasa has been chosen as the MVP of this tournament,</i>

02:27.430 --> 02:31.330
<i>and also holds the title of top goalscorer, with 31 goals.</i>

02:31.330 --> 02:34.620
<i>Honey, Tsubasa won!</i>

02:34.620 --> 02:36.250
He did it, Roberto!

02:36.950 --> 02:38.650
Oh?

02:38.650 --> 02:39.760
Roberto?

02:39.760 --> 02:45.810
<i>And Tsubasa's partner Misaki has provided the highest number of assists, paving the way for 15 goals in total.</i>

02:45.810 --> 02:49.930
god have mercy on my soul while tl'ing that screen for the

02:45.810 --> 02:49.930
<i>Here on the screen are the top 20 players of the tournament!</i>

02:49.930 --> 02:55.400
<i>Certainly, these boys will carry Japanese football into the future.</i>

02:56.770 --> 02:59.690
Tsubasa, can you tell us how you feel about winning?

02:59.690 --> 03:01.560
Of course! I am really happy!

03:01.560 --> 03:03.780
With this tournament win, what's your next dream?

03:03.780 --> 03:07.290
I am going to Brazil with Roberto!

03:10.340 --> 03:12.720
Well, we were the runner-ups!

03:12.720 --> 03:14.360
Go home with your heads held high!

03:14.360 --> 03:15.280
Yes!

03:15.280 --> 03:17.500
You played really well.

03:18.780 --> 03:19.670
You...

03:19.670 --> 03:26.180
Kojiro Hyuga, under the conditions we spoke of earlier, I am scouting you for Toho Academy.

03:27.380 --> 03:29.930
But... I lost to Tsubasa...

03:29.930 --> 03:34.440
I am well aware. We also plan to scout Tsubasa.

03:34.440 --> 03:41.440
But we don't plan to use him as a striker, but as a playmaker.

03:34.440 --> 03:36.720
You did it Tsubasa!

03:36.720 --> 03:37.980
Congratulations!

03:37.980 --> 03:38.940
Thanks!

03:38.940 --> 03:41.440
You really did it.

03:41.440 --> 03:46.550
Hyuga, the one we're scouting as our ace striker... is you.

03:46.550 --> 03:47.200
What?!

03:47.200 --> 03:52.370
With that, Toho Academy will become invincible in Japan.

03:52.370 --> 03:57.290
You will form the ultimate Golden Duo with Tsubasa.

03:58.440 --> 04:01.680
Tsubasa and I, paired up...?

04:01.680 --> 04:03.420
That's awesome!

04:03.420 --> 04:05.510
No one on earth could defeat that duo, captain!

04:05.510 --> 04:08.720
I trust you'll be joining us, Hyuga?

04:08.720 --> 04:10.720
B-but...

04:10.720 --> 04:13.210
Why are you hesitating?

04:13.210 --> 04:14.740
Go, Kojiro!

04:14.740 --> 04:17.380
Isn't this your dream come true?

04:17.380 --> 04:18.440
Coach...

04:18.440 --> 04:19.780
Bro!

04:19.780 --> 04:20.940
Kojiro!

04:20.940 --> 04:23.190
Guys...

04:23.240 --> 04:26.140
Congratulations on second place, bro!

04:26.140 --> 04:27.990
You did really well, Kojiro!

04:27.990 --> 04:31.900
Your pride is getting the better of you
after this loss to Tsubasa in the finals.

04:31.900 --> 04:34.030
You can give us your reply later.

04:34.030 --> 04:35.060
Let's go.

04:35.060 --> 04:35.790
Okay.

04:36.980 --> 04:38.790
Big bro...

04:42.480 --> 04:48.090
I... I look forward to being a part of Toho Academy.

05:13.540 --> 05:16.790
Misaki, it's almost time to say goodbye, isn't it?

05:17.440 --> 05:18.790
Yeah...

05:23.270 --> 05:24.670
Tsubasa!

05:25.470 --> 05:26.630
Mom!

05:26.630 --> 05:30.340
It's terrible! I found this at the hotel!

05:30.340 --> 05:31.600
What...?

05:31.600 --> 05:37.020
It's Roberto!
Roberto has returned to Brazil without you!

05:37.020 --> 05:38.230
WHAT?!

05:43.320 --> 05:46.320
TO TSUBASA

05:44.850 --> 05:46.320
But why?

05:46.320 --> 05:50.490
He promised me...
Why?

05:50.490 --> 05:53.120
Why did he leave alone?

05:53.120 --> 05:55.540
Guys... why would he do that?

05:55.540 --> 05:56.410
Tsubasa...

05:56.410 --> 06:00.120
Tsubasa, if you leave right now,
you might be able to catch up to him.

06:00.120 --> 06:01.180
Wha—

06:01.180 --> 06:04.880
He's right. You might be able to
catch him at the airport if you hurry up.

06:04.880 --> 06:06.140
Mister!

06:06.140 --> 06:07.090
Got it!

06:15.640 --> 06:17.020
Tsubasa...

06:17.780 --> 06:20.520
<i>Going to Brazil has been your biggest dream.</i>

06:21.160 --> 06:24.790
<i>You have to catch Roberto, Tsubasa.</i>

06:28.190 --> 06:33.450
holy shit that handwriting. RIP, typesetting

06:29.560 --> 06:31.340
<i>"Dear Tsubasa,</i>

06:31.340 --> 06:33.450
<i>Please forgive me, Tsubasa.</i>

06:33.450 --> 06:38.280
<i>I just can't take you to Brazil.</i>

06:38.280 --> 06:42.980
<i>As you already know, I have a problem
with my eyes called retinal detachment,</i>

06:42.980 --> 06:46.160
<i>and because of that, I can't play football anymore.</i>

06:46.160 --> 06:48.260
<i>Playing was my only purpose in life,</i>

06:48.260 --> 06:51.380
<i>so losing that was a huge shock for me.</i>

06:51.380 --> 06:58.160
<i>The one who gave me a new reason for living
when I was so down... was you, Tsubasa.</i>

06:58.220 --> 07:01.730
<i>I was drawn in by your prodigious football sense,</i>

07:01.730 --> 07:06.520
<i>and I wanted to raise you into the best
football player in the world, with my own hands.</i>

07:06.520 --> 07:12.070
<i>But Tsubasa, I can't take you with me to Brazil after all.</i>

07:13.090 --> 07:17.790
<i>If I took you away, I would be tearing the Ozora family apart.</i>

07:17.790 --> 07:21.080
<i>Families are meant to be together.</i>

07:22.720 --> 07:27.170
<i>Although, frankly, the reason I'm not taking you with me is actually much more personal.</i>

07:28.180 --> 07:36.180
<i>No matter the circumstances, as a player who stopped playing football halfway, I'm a loser.</i>

07:36.180 --> 07:40.940
<i>Meanwhile, you are seriously delving
into living your life as a football player.</i>

07:40.940 --> 07:42.690
<i>There's nothing I can teach you.</i>

07:42.690 --> 07:48.900
<i>Even if I could, the more you grew,
the harder your training would get,</i>

07:48.900 --> 07:52.900
<i>and I'm afraid I might lose my eyesight in the process.</i>

07:52.900 --> 07:55.240
<i>By then, it would be too late.</i>

07:55.240 --> 07:58.950
<i>You would be the one shouldering the consequences, Tsubasa.</i>

08:01.000 --> 08:04.070
It won't go through.
He turned off his phone.

08:04.070 --> 08:05.960
I can't get through to him.

08:05.960 --> 08:10.210
<i>Roberto...
You are not a loser!</i>

08:10.210 --> 08:16.890
<i>The one who taught me football, "the true football," was you, Roberto!</i>

08:19.180 --> 08:20.220
<i>Tsubasa...</i>

08:20.220 --> 08:24.690
<i>Even if you stay here in Japan,
I'm sure you'll grow to be an excellent player.</i>

08:25.360 --> 08:29.110
<i>Even without me, I'm sure you will.</i>

08:29.950 --> 08:32.990
<i>I will return to Brazil, alone.</i>

08:32.990 --> 08:37.110
<i>I will be parting with you forever, here and now.</i>

08:37.710 --> 08:38.740
<i>Tsubasa...</i>

08:39.900 --> 08:40.870
<i>Farewell.</i>

08:51.670 --> 08:56.880
<i>I worked so hard to go to Brazil with Roberto.</i>

08:58.640 --> 09:01.620
<i>I won, just like I promised I would!</i>

09:03.850 --> 09:06.350
<i>Why are you going back alone?</i>

09:20.030 --> 09:21.160
<i>Roberto!</i>

09:24.580 --> 09:25.790
<i>Roberto...</i>

09:28.160 --> 09:29.790
<i>Roberto!</i>

09:33.520 --> 09:34.550
<i>Roberto!</i>

09:39.720 --> 09:40.890
<i>Roberto...</i>

09:41.690 --> 09:42.940
<i>Why?</i>

09:45.260 --> 09:47.890
Why are you leaving without me?!

09:47.890 --> 09:51.040
Roberto!

10:00.070 --> 10:03.910
— A FEW DAYS AFTER THE NATIONAL YOUTH FOOTBALL TOURNAMENT, NANKATSU CITY —

10:03.910 --> 10:05.830
FOR RENT

10:03.910 --> 10:05.830
EIYU REAL ESTATE

10:14.170 --> 10:16.210
Taro, are you done packing?

10:17.640 --> 10:19.300
Yup, I'm all set.

10:20.100 --> 10:21.430
Let's depart, then.

10:22.240 --> 10:23.550
Sure.

10:23.550 --> 10:25.260
NANKATSU CITY NANKATSU ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

10:25.260 --> 10:27.060
FOOTBALL CLUB

10:27.060 --> 10:30.060
and holy shit how are gonna typeset that ball?

10:27.660 --> 10:29.180
Sorry for the trouble, guys!

10:29.180 --> 10:31.550
I made you come all the way to Nankatsu Elementary.

10:31.550 --> 10:32.980
Don't worry about it.

10:32.980 --> 10:37.700
Misaki is one of our cherished teammates
from Nankatsu SC, after all.

10:37.700 --> 10:40.320
I got Wakabayashi to sign it, too.

10:40.320 --> 10:43.710
He said he'll be there to see Misaki off.

10:43.710 --> 10:46.730
So Tsubasa didn't come today either, huh?

10:46.730 --> 10:50.740
Yeah, he apparently shut himself in his room from the shock.

10:50.740 --> 10:52.630
Well, I guess he would.

10:52.630 --> 10:56.780
I wonder what he'll do now that Roberto is gone.

10:58.480 --> 10:59.910
I heard the news.

10:59.910 --> 11:03.600
Didn't Tsubasa get scouted by Toho Academy?

11:03.600 --> 11:04.620
Yeah.

11:04.620 --> 11:06.040
That's awesome.

11:06.040 --> 11:09.360
To think someone from the prestigious
Toho Academy would scout you...

11:09.360 --> 11:12.230
He hasn't decided to go there yet, you know!

11:12.230 --> 11:15.960
He might just attend Nankatsu Junior High!

11:15.960 --> 11:21.320
Well, with his abilities, it would be a waste
to attend Nankatsu, a mere public school.

11:21.320 --> 11:28.830
If Tsubasa goes to Nankatsu, we'd be able to settle things with him as Shutetsu, though.

11:30.320 --> 11:32.240
What's wrong, Takasugi?

11:32.240 --> 11:39.220
Well, I just realized Nankatsu SC will be
separated once we start junior high.

11:41.620 --> 11:47.930
That's precisely why our farewell gift for
Misaki must have Tsubasa's part on it.

11:51.930 --> 11:53.690
Are you sure, Taro?

11:53.690 --> 11:55.440
You've lied to them.

11:56.190 --> 11:57.040
Yeah...

11:59.730 --> 12:01.520
Misaki!

12:01.520 --> 12:02.240
What?!

12:03.210 --> 12:04.240
Guys!

12:04.240 --> 12:06.920
What's with all that luggage?!

12:06.920 --> 12:09.330
Weren't you going to leave tomorrow?

12:09.960 --> 12:11.180
Sorry.

12:11.180 --> 12:14.710
I just really thought it'd be hard
to leave if I saw you guys again...

12:14.710 --> 12:16.790
That's cold, Misaki!

12:16.790 --> 12:18.460
Sorry...

12:18.460 --> 12:20.620
Well then, Ishizaki, we need to hurry up.

12:20.620 --> 12:21.840
Oh yeah!

12:21.840 --> 12:23.920
Misaki, which bus are you taking?

12:25.010 --> 12:27.090
The one coming in 15 minutes.

12:27.090 --> 12:28.310
Damn!

12:28.310 --> 12:31.230
Okay! I'll run over to Tsubasa's really quick.

12:31.230 --> 12:33.250
Let's call Wakabayashi, too.

12:33.250 --> 12:35.020
All right.

12:36.150 --> 12:38.020
Guys...

12:38.720 --> 12:40.270
Huh?! He's not home?!

12:40.270 --> 12:43.680
I think he's by the riverside today, as well.

12:43.680 --> 12:44.780
Did anything happen?

12:44.780 --> 12:47.240
Misaki is leaving today!

12:47.240 --> 12:48.410
What?!

12:54.270 --> 13:02.170
<i>Advanced level dribbling, a new shooting technique, effective training menu...</i>

13:02.170 --> 13:09.600
<i>The notebook you left for me has all the things I will need from now on.</i>

13:09.600 --> 13:10.550
<i>But...</i>

13:13.890 --> 13:19.480
<i>Roberto, I wanted to go to Brazil after all.</i>

13:19.480 --> 13:21.440
Tsubasa!

13:23.810 --> 13:24.940
Ishizaki...?

13:24.940 --> 13:26.830
It's bad, Tsubasa!

13:26.830 --> 13:27.950
Misaki is...

13:31.720 --> 13:35.080
Oh, the bus is here.

13:42.470 --> 13:45.560
Ishizaki, you're taking too long...

13:47.050 --> 13:49.300
Taro, it's time to go.

13:49.300 --> 13:50.580
Okay.

13:51.390 --> 13:53.390
See you all, then.

13:53.390 --> 13:55.390
Are you really going, Misaki?

13:55.390 --> 13:56.600
Yeah.

13:56.600 --> 13:59.350
Give my regards to Tsubasa, as well.

14:02.150 --> 14:03.820
See you again, Misaki.

14:03.820 --> 14:05.240
Misaki, take care of yourself.

14:05.240 --> 14:06.680
Farewell.

14:09.150 --> 14:10.910
Take care of yourself!

14:10.910 --> 14:12.550
same things in chorus

14:12.560 --> 14:13.410
Oh!

14:14.800 --> 14:16.100
Misaki!

14:16.100 --> 14:16.910
Oh...

14:23.380 --> 14:25.380
Tsubasa!

14:25.380 --> 14:27.630
Misaki!

14:29.130 --> 14:31.640
Misaki!

14:31.640 --> 14:33.180
top ten anime dramas

14:33.260 --> 14:35.180
Tsubasa, farewell!

14:35.180 --> 14:36.930
Stay safe and well!

14:36.930 --> 14:38.770
Tsubasa.

14:39.940 --> 14:42.940
Catch this, Misaki!

14:49.320 --> 14:52.780
<i>Let's form a duo in the National Team as well.
- Tsubasa Ozora</i>

14:53.200 --> 14:54.780
Misaki.

14:58.300 --> 15:00.290
Thank you, Tsubasa!

15:00.290 --> 15:02.790
Thank you guys!

15:09.180 --> 15:12.420
<i>Farewell...
Farewell, Misaki!</i>

15:13.900 --> 15:15.970
Misaki had his departure as well, huh?

15:16.660 --> 15:17.850
Wakabayashi.

15:18.320 --> 15:19.470
Wakabayashi.

15:20.350 --> 15:22.060
What do you mean by "as well"?

15:22.060 --> 15:25.900
Tsubasa, I'm headed to Germany.

15:28.340 --> 15:32.200
<i>You will become a junior high student next year, huh, Genzo?</i>

15:32.200 --> 15:33.070
<i>Yeah.</i>

15:34.270 --> 15:40.430
<i>To be frank, it seems this might be
the last year I'll be able to coach you.</i>

15:41.080 --> 15:43.820
<i>The Japanese Football Federation has asked me</i>

15:43.820 --> 15:48.730
<i>if I would like to participate in an induction course in Germany.</i>

15:48.730 --> 15:53.220
<i>I really want to go, for the sake of improving the level of Japanese football.</i>

15:53.220 --> 15:55.470
<i>That's...</i>

15:56.080 --> 15:58.440
<i>Starting from spring of next year,</i>

15:58.440 --> 16:04.480
<i>for two years— and for longer,
if possible— I want to see European football.</i>

16:04.480 --> 16:10.230
<i>So with that in mind, Genzo, won't you come to Germany with me?</i>

16:10.230 --> 16:12.240
<i>Huh?</i>

16:13.740 --> 16:16.030
So you are going to Germany?

16:16.030 --> 16:22.040
After I heard you were going to Brazil, I started thinking, too.

16:22.040 --> 16:24.900
If my aim is to become a world-class player,

16:24.900 --> 16:27.540
I should see how football is played in the rest of the world.

16:27.540 --> 16:32.000
The German league is one of the top leagues in the world,

16:32.000 --> 16:35.540
and it's produced many wonderful goalkeepers.

16:35.540 --> 16:38.370
The place I should go is Germany.

16:38.370 --> 16:41.060
I'm aiming to be the best goalkeeper in the world.

16:41.060 --> 16:43.310
Wakabayashi.

16:46.100 --> 16:47.800
Do your best and come back.

16:47.800 --> 16:52.020
You can definitely become the best goalkeeper, Wakabayashi.

16:52.020 --> 16:53.990
Yeah, I will do my best.

16:53.990 --> 16:59.830
But before that, Tsubasa, would you
accept another challenge from me?

16:59.830 --> 17:02.830
Sure, I would love to.

17:03.040 --> 17:07.040
ONE WEEK LATER

17:13.340 --> 17:18.340
Our first encounter and our first battle
was also on this field, Wakabayashi.

17:19.060 --> 17:21.850
It sure was, Tsubasa.

17:22.300 --> 17:23.370
Come, Tsubasa.

17:23.370 --> 17:25.040
It will be a one play battle.

17:25.040 --> 17:26.100
All right!

17:26.100 --> 17:27.580
Tsubasa.

17:27.580 --> 17:29.100
Wakabayashi.

17:30.130 --> 17:31.110
Here I come!

17:36.240 --> 17:38.070
Take this, Wakabayashi!

17:38.950 --> 17:41.950
<i>I won't let anyone score from beyond the penalty area— even you!</i>

17:47.160 --> 17:48.830
It went past him!

17:49.580 --> 17:51.080
No, it hit the post!

17:52.750 --> 17:53.710
Tsubasa!

18:02.910 --> 18:04.470
He caught it!

18:13.690 --> 18:15.780
Well, that's Wakabayashi for you.

18:17.040 --> 18:18.780
It was just luck.

18:18.780 --> 18:22.030
The ball just happened to be going where I jumped haphazardly.

18:31.120 --> 18:34.300
Tsubasa, until I become a professional player in Germany,

18:34.300 --> 18:36.360
I don't plan on returning to Japan.

18:38.510 --> 18:42.010
Wakabayashi, I...

18:47.340 --> 18:49.980
I will attend Nankatsu Junior High with everyone.

18:50.780 --> 18:52.480
That's it!

18:52.480 --> 18:54.360
He said Nankatsu!

18:54.360 --> 18:57.570
I can play even more with Tsubasa.

18:57.570 --> 18:59.630
I haven't given up on my dreams.

18:59.630 --> 19:04.010
In Nankatsu Junior High, I will fight along
with everyone and, someday, go to Brazil.

19:04.010 --> 19:04.990
Is that so?

19:04.990 --> 19:09.020
Then, next time we meet,
we will be Japanese National Team members.

19:09.020 --> 19:09.500
Sure.

19:17.660 --> 19:21.880
<i>Goodbye until then, Tsubasa.</i>

19:26.100 --> 19:28.930
— 3 YEARS LATER —

19:30.350 --> 19:34.910
<i>Genzo Wakabayashi continued to make impressive saves one after another in the last match.</i>

19:34.910 --> 19:39.690
<i>He is getting closer once again to
becoming the regular goalkeeper of the B team.</i>

19:40.900 --> 19:43.160
<i>{hmph!}That's how it should be.</i>

19:46.540 --> 19:48.540
Hey, Ishizaki!

19:48.540 --> 19:49.580
What's up?

19:49.580 --> 19:51.830
Did you enjoy your spring break?

19:51.830 --> 19:55.330
Nankatsu Junior High Football Club 3rd Grader
Ryo Ishizaki

19:51.830 --> 19:54.680
Look, you might call it spring break, but all we did was

19:54.680 --> 19:59.290
win through the prefecture tournament and become champion again.

19:59.290 --> 20:03.470
There is no way I can enjoy a 3-day break, you know.

20:03.470 --> 20:05.220
Sign: Teppei Kisugi

20:03.470 --> 20:05.470
I guess that's true.

20:05.470 --> 20:11.300
With Tsubasa on the team, losing early
and having a long break is an impossibility.

20:05.640 --> 20:08.220
Sign: Mamoru Izawa

20:08.310 --> 20:10.600
Sign: Hajime Taki

20:10.680 --> 20:12.980
Sign: Shingo Takasugi

20:11.300 --> 20:12.980
You don't hold back.

20:12.980 --> 20:19.320
Idiot! Tsubasa joined a training camp for high school tryouts for 3 days, right as the tournament ended!

20:17.780 --> 20:19.320
Good morning, Sanae!

20:19.320 --> 20:21.440
Good morning!

20:19.320 --> 20:21.440
Nankatsu Junior High Football Club Manager 3rd Grader
Sanae Nakazawa.

20:21.440 --> 20:32.080
Nankatsu SC's core players Izawa, Kisugi, Taki and Takasugi enrolled in Nankatsu Junior High to aim for new heights with Tsubasa.

20:32.080 --> 20:35.040
Yuzo Morisaki / Masato Nakazato / Kenichi Iwami

20:32.080 --> 20:38.240
Nankatsu has grown to become the leading champion team in junior high football, despite being a public school.

20:36.170 --> 20:38.920
Tsuyoshi Oda / Hiroshi Nagano

20:38.240 --> 20:44.620
On the other side, Urabe, Kishida, Nishio and Nakaya, who were also members of Nankatsu SC,

20:44.620 --> 20:46.630
decided to join Otomo Junior High,

20:46.630 --> 20:50.430
instead choosing to fight against Nankatsu, led by Tsubasa Ozora.

20:52.180 --> 20:53.680
TOHO ACADEMY FOOTBALL GROUND

20:52.180 --> 20:52.930
Get there!

20:52.930 --> 20:53.680
Go!

20:53.680 --> 20:55.020
Run!

20:53.680 --> 20:56.440
Toho Academy Junior High

20:55.020 --> 20:56.440
What are you doing?!

20:56.440 --> 20:58.560
Treat the ball with care!

20:58.560 --> 21:02.570
Toho Academy Junior High Football Club Captain 3rd Grader
Kojiro Hyuga.

20:58.560 --> 21:02.570
At this rate, we won't be able to beat
Nankatsu Junior High again this year!

21:02.570 --> 21:06.070
Toho Academy Junior High Football Club 3rd Grader
Ken Wakashimazu

21:02.570 --> 21:06.070
<i>Yeah, this year, we will dethrone Tsubasa Ozora!</i>

21:06.070 --> 21:08.070
Hyuga.

21:08.070 --> 21:11.080
Let me introduce you to a new student.

21:11.580 --> 21:14.080
Toho Academy Junior High Football Club 1st Grader
Takeshi Sawada

21:11.800 --> 21:14.080
It's nice to see you again, Hyuga!

21:14.820 --> 21:16.460
So you've come, Takeshi!

21:16.460 --> 21:17.710
Yes, sir!

21:17.710 --> 21:20.980
All right! Now we have all the members we need.

21:20.980 --> 21:23.930
Our Toho Academy will be the one that shatters

21:23.930 --> 21:26.910
Nankatsu's dreams of a third consecutive championship!

21:26.910 --> 21:28.090
Yeah!

21:30.100 --> 21:31.820
Do your best, guys!

21:31.820 --> 21:33.930
Five minutes left in the first half.

21:38.940 --> 21:42.520
Nankatsu Junior High Football Club Captain 3rd Grader
Tsubasa Ozora

21:39.980 --> 21:42.520
Let's enjoy ourselves!

21:42.520 --> 21:43.880
Tsubasa!

21:43.880 --> 21:46.280
So you're back, Tsubasa?

21:47.440 --> 21:47.990
Here we go!

21:49.590 --> 21:53.020
Nankatsu Junior High's Captain, Tsubasa Ozora.

21:53.020 --> 21:57.580
He aims to be the first three consecutive championship winner ever in junior high football.

21:57.580 --> 22:04.090
Tsubasa Ozora and Kojiro Hyuga,
old rivals going against each other once more.

22:05.210 --> 22:07.870
They might just change the course of Japanese football.

22:07.870 --> 22:11.300
No... they have to.

22:13.860 --> 22:15.440
Let's go, guys!

22:15.440 --> 22:16.880
Yeah!

22:38.830 --> 22:44.710
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.830 --> 22:44.710
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.710 --> 22:50.720
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.710 --> 22:50.720
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.720 --> 22:56.720
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.720 --> 22:56.720
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.720 --> 23:02.190
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.720 --> 23:02.190
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:08.320
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:08.320
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:15.030
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:15.030
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.030 --> 23:21.080
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.080 --> 23:26.090
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.080 --> 23:26.090
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.380 --> 23:33.260
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.380 --> 23:33.260
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.260 --> 23:39.140
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.140 --> 23:46.020
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.140 --> 23:46.020
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.110 --> 24:00.760
COMING UP, EPISODE 29:
START OF SUMMER!
